title: Keep a refunded asset account frozen or blocked

doc:
- audience: [Runtime Dev, Runtime User]
  description: |-
    `pallet_assets::refund` removed the asset account even when it was frozen or blocked, so the
    holder could burn their balance, drop the `Frozen` or `Blocked` status together with the
    entry and receive the asset again afterwards, free to move it. Refunding a frozen or blocked
    account now burns the balance and returns the deposit or consumer reference as before, but
    keeps a zero-balance entry that stays frozen or blocked until the admin thaws it, which
    removes the entry. A holder can therefore still free a consumer reference forced on them by
    an asset owner, but can no longer lift a freeze or block. Such an entry has the new
    `ExistenceReason::Tombstone` and cannot receive the asset, whatever its status. It still
    counts in `AssetDetails::accounts`, so the owner cannot raise the minimum balance while it
    exists, and `thaw` fails with `ContainsHolds` or `ContainsFreezes` while it has a hold or
    freeze.

    To back this entry with a deposit, `freeze` and `block` now reserve `AssetAccountDeposit`
    from the freezer when the account's holder can refund it, that is when it exists through a
    consumer reference or its own deposit, or is already a tombstone. The deposit is recorded in
    the new `FreezerDeposits` storage item and returned to the account that placed it when the
    account is thawed or destroyed together with the asset. Freezing or blocking an account that
    already has a freezer deposit takes no further deposit, and the freezer must hold enough
    free balance for it. Accounts that exist as `Sufficient` or through a deposit someone else
    placed cannot be refunded while frozen or blocked and take no freezer deposit. Accounts
    frozen or blocked before this change hold no freezer deposit until they are frozen or
    blocked again. No migration is needed: `FreezerDeposits` starts empty and `Tombstone` is a
    new variant.

    `WeightInfo` gains `destroy_blocked_accounts`, which prices `destroy_accounts` for accounts
    that return a freezer deposit. The `destroy_accounts` call is charged the larger of the two
    weights, since an account is either reaped through the asset or returns a freezer deposit.

crates:
- name: pallet-assets
  bump: major
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: minor
- name: asset-hub-rococo-runtime
  bump: minor
